/data/repository/issue {"number": 637, "updatedAt": "2026-10-20T06:24:11Z", "title": "Web: retry failed administrator loading without changing the payer-transfer organisation", "url": "https://github.com/getsotto/sotto/issues/637", "state": "OPEN", "stateReason": null, "author": {"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132019073?u=19cb240001b907168b9e766bced89600568c8523&v=4", "login": "Maxerns", "id": "U_kgDOB95zgQ", "profileUrl": "https://github.com/Maxerns", "name": null, "__typename": "User"}, "body": "## What happens\n\nIn **Change who pays**, choosing an organisation loads its members so the user can select the other payer's administrator. If that request fails, the form says:\n\n> The transfer service is temporarily unavailable. Try again shortly.\n\nHowever, the administrator selector contains only its placeholder, **Review payer transfer** is disabled, and there is no retry action. The selected organisation remains unchanged. Users must discover that clearing and reselecting it starts another request, or reload the page.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nVerified on main `07f32e5cbdc758ddebfbc8a431302b93d2daa98a`, macOS arm64, Node 24.15.0, Vitest 5.0.0 / happy-dom, using a temporary component probe in a clean checkout:\n\n1. Render the real `PersonalTransferStart` with synthetic available capabilities, a signed-in account and an organisation `org-b`.\n2. Make the first `fetchMembers(\"org-b\")` reject with `Error(\"server error (503)\")`; configure the next call to return one owner.\n3. Choose `org-b`. Observe the error, the empty administrator selector, the disabled review button and the absence of a retry control. The members API has been called once.\n4. Choose the blank organisation option and then `org-b` again. The owner loads; selecting them enables **Review payer transfer**.\n\nThe probe passed against unchanged production code and was removed after verification. It made no quote, transfer or payment request. All APIs were mocked; no live account or native browser journey was exercised.\n\n## Expected behaviour\n\nAfter administrator discovery fails, users can explicitly retry for the currently selected organisation without changing that selection or reloading the page.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A failed members request exposes a clearly labelled retry control for the selected organisation, alongside the existing accessible error.\n- [ ] Retry preserves the selected organisation, clears the previous discovery error while loading and prevents overlapping retry requests. It does not fetch a quote or create a transfer.\n- [ ] A successful retry repopulates eligible administrator choices and removes the recovery control/error. Selecting an administrator enables the existing review flow.\n- [ ] A second failure restores the retry control. A successful empty result is not presented as a request failure.\n- [ ] Changing or clearing the organisation clears recovery state associated with the old selection. Keep member-discovery errors distinct from quote/submission errors so those failures do not offer the wrong retry action.\n- [ ] Add component tests for initial failure, pending retry, repeated failure and recovery using deferred promises and synthetic fixtures; pass the web test suite.\n\n## Starting points\n\n- [`PersonalTransferStart` in PayerTransferStart.tsx](https://github.com/getsotto/sotto/blob/07f32e5cbdc758ddebfbc8a431302b93d2daa98a/web/src/PayerTransferStart.tsx): `chooseOrganisation`, `members`, the shared error state and the rendered controls.\n- [`PayerTransferJourneys.test.tsx`](https://github.com/getsotto/sotto/blob/07f32e5cbdc758ddebfbc8a431302b93d2daa98a/web/src/__tests__/PayerTransferJourneys.test.tsx): existing API mocks and organisation/member fixtures.\n\nKeep this scoped to administrator discovery in the personal transfer-start form. No transfer authority, billing rules, server API or sponsored-transfer changes are needed. Open/closed issues and open PRs were checked for overlap; #635 covers inbox pagination, not this form.\n\nSuitable for a first contribution using the existing React state and test patterns. Follow `CONTRIBUTING.md`, including DCO sign-off (`git commit -s`).\n", "bodyHTML": "<h2 dir=\"auto\">What happens</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In <strong>Change who pays</strong>, choosing an organisation loads its members so the user can select the other payer's administrator. If that request fails, the form says:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The transfer service is temporarily unavailable. Try again shortly.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">However, the administrator selector contains only its placeholder, <strong>Review payer transfer</strong> is disabled, and there is no retry action. The selected organisation remains unchanged. Users must discover that clearing and reselecting it starts another request, or reload the page.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Reproduction</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Verified on main <code class=\"notranslate\">07f32e5cbdc758ddebfbc8a431302b93d2daa98a</code>, macOS arm64, Node 24.15.0, Vitest 5.0.0 / happy-dom, using a temporary component probe in a clean checkout:</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Render the real <code class=\"notranslate\">PersonalTransferStart</code> with synthetic available capabilities, a signed-in account and an organisation <code class=\"notranslate\">org-b</code>.</li>\n<li>Make the first <code class=\"notranslate\">fetchMembers(\"org-b\")</code> reject with <code class=\"notranslate\">Error(\"server error (503)\")</code>; configure the next call to return one owner.</li>\n<li>Choose <code class=\"notranslate\">org-b</code>. Observe the error, the empty administrator selector, the disabled review button and the absence of a retry control. The members API has been called once.</li>\n<li>Choose the blank organisation option and then <code class=\"notranslate\">org-b</code> again. The owner loads; selecting them enables <strong>Review payer transfer</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The probe passed against unchanged production code and was removed after verification. It made no quote, transfer or payment request. All APIs were mocked; no live account or native browser journey was exercised.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Expected behaviour</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">After administrator discovery fails, users can explicitly retry for the currently selected organisation without changing that selection or reloading the page.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Acceptance criteria</h2>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> A failed members request exposes a clearly labelled retry control for the selected organisation, alongside the existing accessible error.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Retry preserves the selected organisation, clears the previous discovery error while loading
